    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d124-a2">

                <pb facs="0249" n="157" sameAs="frus:frus1899/pg157"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Conger to the Tsungli yamen</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States of America</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                rendition="#italic">Pekin, China</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1898-12-20"><hi rendition="#italic">December
                                20, 1898</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>In reference to the antiforeign sentiment in the province of Shantung and the
                    general annoyance it is causing the missionaries and native Christians therein
                    residing, and in order that your highness and your excellencies may be more
                    fully advised as to the real situation, the undersigned, envoy extraordinary and
                    minister plenipotentiary of the United States of America, has the honor to
                    transmit herewith, without comment or suggestion, a copy of a statement made by
                    Charles A. Killie, William S. Faris, and William P. Chalfant, three American
                    missionaries, detailing a very serious experience which they recently had in the
                    north of that province.</p>
                <p>The undersigned avails, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">E. H. Conger</hi>.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
